winemac: one switch for the Metal HUD

macOS adds a "Metal HUD" menu of its own to a program started with MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1, with a
Show HUD / Hide HUD item. That item does nothing once a layer's own HUD setting has been made,
and View > Show/Hide Metal HUD worked by making that setting, so the system's item was dead.
The two are now tied together: the system's item is the switch, the layers are set to what it
says (checked every second and when a menu closes), and the View item and the shortcuts press
it. Its title is only brought up to date by menuNeedsUpdate:, which is asked for before it is
read. The shortcut shown in the menu is Control-Command-H, which needs no function key;
Option-F12 still works.

